From b78124e4077ffb0fcc4e0ddebeea64f4d9bf2a36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminusfilms <steve@terminusfilms.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 16:04:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Public API: enforce the project discoverable flag

The public API (v0 and v1) served any project's records to anyone who
knew (or enumerated) a record UUID or project id, regardless of the
project's discoverable setting. The v1 show-by-uuid path had no project
scoping at all.

A shared DiscoverableProjectScope concern filters the requested
project_ids down to discoverable projects:

- V1 PublicController: every branch of base_query is scoped to
  discoverable projects; the show-by-uuid branch additionally requires
  the record to be owned by or shared with a requested project.
- V0 PublicController: same scoping for list and nested routes.
- Manifests (v0 + v1): manifest queries require a discoverable project,
  including the single-manifest path that previously had no project
  filter when called without project_ids.
- Project descriptors (v0 + v1): 404 for non-discoverable projects
  (previously leaked the full model/field schema of any project).

Records in non-discoverable projects now return 404/empty from every
public endpoint; discoverable projects are unaffected.

